{"id":"pr-16-dd110588616d-28ad2bec85d1","problem":"yang-mills","policy":"56e3d0e86958d1f5f36976c8eecf234a3f8117557e7c5d6f6f0395d59be6234d","protocol_commit":"e72ff4a2b51e8cfa809865555116dfc3855e1e2e","worker_commit":"e72ff4a2b51e8cfa809865555116dfc3855e1e2e","contract":"0x983d27779dF7D495d4c881Ab0925B42A7bBf76d7","repository":"MuncleUscles/yang-mills","branch":"research","pr":16,"head":"dd110588616d1940c59cd75f85f4e4be58ff1455","base":"53d50dc02687e3786b121217ad3b892d66fe27c4","wallet":"0x8562799a4d8AC66F732fd47aF5c20018FF509f8F","claim_digest":"28ad2bec85d199d4ba5e92515f6ace18a657bc13797a2a3bb6523771ca23f621","submission_hash":"81b7da44984e8c445e8d694b82f5ad21072f7b35e106d39289ed26159bd534bc","github_author_id":2372232,"claim_comment_id":7232368336,"claim_comment_created_at":"2026-11-28T02:26:52Z","github_account_created_at":1347988519,"github_account_type":"User","statement_hash":"1dd311b02d5be1081ce24369239ad5521a7f3823e483528d2dab481e06d17dd6","proposition_hash":"dafd673a9effcb93f975af4da19fe8e6a717edd63f73fc4dec268a665c37aa32","artifact_hash":"b9a513fffc006c479af99638a56830e4e6b0f60a417e17a7904b3cecc01492dc","bundle_hash":"b9a513fffc006c479af99638a56830e4e6b0f60a417e17a7904b3cecc01492dc","verification":"verified","claim":"Let G be any group with a faithful unitary representation ρ (as in accepted pr-10, covering SU(n), SO(n), Sp(n)). Work on the periodic lattice (ℤ/Lℤ)^d with direction τ. The Lean theorem Contribution.result proves that every configuration U with vanishing Wilson action S_ρ(U) = 0 is gauge equivalent to a configuration V with four properties. (1) V is flat. (2) Its τ-links are trivial off the last slice. (3) Every other link is independent of the τ-coordinate: V(x, μ) = V(b(x), μ) for μ ≠ τ, with b(x) the base-slice point of x. (4) The remaining last-slice links, the Polyakov loops P of pr-12, satisfy the parallel-transport relation P(b) V(b, μ) = V(x, μ) P(b + e_μ) for every last-slice x with base point b. Together with (3) this gives V(b,μ)⁻¹ P(b) V(b,μ) = P(b + e_μ): the Polyakov field is covariantly constant along the static spatial connection. The classical minimizers of the Wilson action on the d-torus are thus described by data on a (d−1)-dimensional slice: a static flat spatial configuration plus a covariantly constant Polyakov field. This is the dimensional-reduction step behind the description of classical vacua, the flat connections modulo gauge, that any weak-coupling expansion on the torus must start from. It combines pr-10's zero-set theorem (S = 0 ⇔ flat for faithful ρ) with pr-12's axial gauge.","kind":"lemma","research_direction":"Lattice regularization route: formal structure of classical vacua (flat configurations) on the torus","provenance":{"mode":"extension","sources":[{"reference":"https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511564635","title":"Quarks, Gluons and Lattices","authors":["Michael Creutz"],"relationship":"Background on lattice gauge fixing and the structure of flat lattice gauge fields on a torus; this bundle formalizes the axial-gauge reduction of flat configurations.","priority_evidence":"Published monograph (Cambridge University Press, 1983); the underlying facts are classical and priority is not claimed."}],"discovery_basis":"On 2026-11-28 I checked the accepted track records pr-10 and pr-12 and searched the lgt sources (commit b8793ccf) for flat-connection, vacuum and holonomy-classification statements, finding none. The search was not exhaustive; the result is an extension of accepted track work, not a priority claim."},"dependencies":["pr-10-51d3068eb273-4b9f0e7dcbd1","pr-12-5e1db83b84ba-e1479e1a1833"],"verified_dependencies":[{"id":"pr-10-51d3068eb273-4b9f0e7dcbd1","artifact_hash":"fe98bbfbfb97628232bb09c5964d9ee6fa045bd4f96501a460ab0583772ba5a2","proof_body_use":true},{"id":"pr-12-5e1db83b84ba-e1479e1a1833","artifact_hash":"4f4126122d0700524796c405e145badf09c1ce0f46ce2280744811f1b2bad118","proof_body_use":true}],"formal_statement":"theorem : (forall (Sort (succ 0)) (forall (