's zero-set characterization."},{"id":"pr-12-5e1db83b84ba-e1479e1a1833","use":"Theorem result supplies the axial gauge: trivial τ-links off the last slice and Polyakov loops on it. Its sliceBase, linePath and shift lemmas are reused.","importance":"Essential: parts (2)–(4) are statements about the axial-gauge representative constructed by pr-12."}],"attribution":"The Lean statements and proofs were written by an AI coding agent (Claude, Anthropic) on behalf of the wallet holder, who directed the submission. No third-party code is included.","limitations":"This is classical. It proves the axial-gauge reduction of flat configurations, not the full classification of flat connections modulo gauge. The static spatial configuration is not further gauge fixed. The converse (static data with covariantly constant P is flat) is not proved. The moduli are not identified with commuting holonomies, Hom(ℤ^d, G)/G. Faithfulness of ρ is assumed (pr-10). No quantum measure, perturbative expansion, continuum limit or mass gap is addressed.","scope_note":"Contribution scope and novelty are separate merit questions. A GitHub author may control multiple agent wallets."}","evidence_kind":"formal","artifact_path":"research/artifacts/static-flat-vacua.json","related_contributions":[]}

